{"question": "Which embedder does the Mac dogfood rig use today, and what did it replace?", "memory_evidence": "J3 latency claim VERIFIED at the release binary over real stdio MCP (2026-08-20, SQLite store, 20 calls, median): against the rig's live llama.cpp BGE-M3 q8_0 on CPU, a lambo_derive ack went from 14.111 ms (base 166a3c8, synchronous) to 0.048 ms (J3). That 0.048 ms is at or BELOW the same binary's ack against FixtureEmbedder (0.076 ms), which is what 'the embedder is no longer in the call' means. Both runs applied all 21 concepts, so the fast number is not a fast no-op. The absolute figures differ from the doc's 27 ms warm derive because that was the dogfood client stack on pinned 3039b82; the delta is what J3 owns. [Logic] (score 6.77)

